  "body": "## What was wrong\n\nMCC has five local short-circuit rules that answer a request inside the proxy without contacting a provider. **Nothing recorded that this had happened**, so the entire layer was unmeasurable — the only way to find out whether it had ever fired was to decompress every stored prompt in a 153,198-row production log and replay the detectors by hand.\n\nThat measurement is what motivates this PR:\n\n| rule | fires, lifetime | input tokens never sent |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `title_generation_skip` | 3,122 | ~14.3M |\n| `suggestion_mode_skip` | 130 | ~1.0M |\n| `quota_mock` | 0 | — |\n| `prefix_detection` | 0 | — |\n| `filepath_extraction_mock` | 0 | — |\n\nThree defects, all invisible for the same reason.\n\n**1. A locally-answered row named a provider.** `set_routing` runs before the intercepts, so the row recorded the provider the request *would* have gone to. In the production log that is **3,246 phantom requests spread across six real providers**, dragging their per-provider averages with them:\n\n```\nnous_portal   2,730     opencode  164     open_router     40\ncommandcode     214     nvidia_nim 58     chatgpt_oauth   40\n```\n\n**2. The reported usage was invented.** Every rule returned a hardcoded `input_tokens=100` / `output_tokens=5` regardless of the request, and those counts reach the client and feed its own accounting. Part IV §1 bans exactly this.\n\n**3. The suggestion-mode trigger scanned the whole transcript.** Any user message containing `[SUGGESTION MODE:` *anywhere in history* answered the request with an empty string — the worst failure this module can produce, because the caller asked a real question and got nothing.\n\n## What this does\n\n- Adds `requests.optimization` (the rule that answered) and `requests.optimization_tokens_saved` (input tokens kept off the wire). Both NULL on an ordinary request.\n- Clears `provider`/`resolved_model` on an optimized row. `requested_model` and `route_chain` still record what *would* have happened, so nothing is lost — only the false claim.\n- Counts usage instead of inventing it. Measured cost of counting (cl100k, this hardware):\n\n```\n  1,500 chars ->     405 tokens     0.5 ms\n 23,000 chars ->   6,241 tokens     7.1 ms   median title prompt\n 76,000 chars ->  20,628 tokens    24.4 ms   typical suggestion prompt\n560,000 chars -> 152,000 tokens   145.9 ms   largest observed\n```\n\nAgainst the multi-second round trip each match avoids, on a path that already calls this counter synchronously for web-tool requests.\n\n- Narrows the suggestion trigger to the trailing user turn. Verified against **all 61** real suggestion requests: the marker is never earlier than **97.61%** into the prompt and is always followed by exactly the same **1,363-character** block, so narrowing loses nothing.\n- Publishes `count_text_tokens`, because `get_token_count` bills fixed per-message framing — right for a request, wrong for a lone reply, which it scores at 4 for the empty string.\n\n`tokens_in`/`tokens_out` stay **NULL, not 0**, on an optimized row: NULL is silence and no provider spoke (§13).\n\n## Verification\n\n**Mutation testing — 6 mutations, each asserted applied, each caught by a named test, no survivors:**\n\n```\nCAUGHT  M1 provider attribution is not cleared\n    FAILED test_request_capture.py::test_local_optimization_row_names_no_provider\nCAUGHT  M2 the rule name is not recorded\nCAUGHT  M3 tokens_saved is not recorded\nCAUGHT  M4 usage goes back to the invented constant\n    FAILED test_optimization_handlers.py::TestUsageIsCountedNotInvented::test_input_tokens_track_the_real_prompt_size\n    FAILED test_optimization_handlers.py::TestUsageIsCountedNotInvented::test_tokens_saved_equals_the_prompt_that_never_went_upstream\nCAUGHT  M5 the reply token count goes back to a constant\nCAUGHT  M6 suggestion trigger scans the whole transcript again\n    FAILED test_detection.py::TestSuggestionModeTrigger::test_marker_only_in_history_does_not_match\n\nsurvivors: none\n```\n\n**Migration against the real prior schema, with an existing row present:**\n\n```\nbefore: has optimization = False (38 columns)\nafter : has optimization = True  (42 columns)\n  new_row: optimization='title_generation_skip' saved=4931 provider=None\n  old_row: optimization=None saved=None provider='nous_portal'\nOK: migrated in place; existing rows keep NULL and are NOT backfilled\n```\n\n**Full suite:** `4,849 passed, 26 skipped, 8 failed`. All 8 are `tests/scripts/test_install_ps1_*` and were **reproduced identically on unmodified `fork/main` in the same shell** — the standing PowerShell installer baseline, not this change.\n\n`ruff format`, `ruff check`, `ty`: clean.\n\n## Deliberately not done\n\n- **No index on the new column.** The dashboard aggregate lands in a later PR, and adding an index changes every neighbouring query's plan (§59). It will be measured then, not guessed at now.\n- **The three never-firing rules are untouched.** They are removed in their own change so this one stays about recording.\n- **No backfill.** The 3,246 historical mis-attributed rows keep their wrong provider. Rewriting history would be worse than the ambiguity; the column marks the boundary from here.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- The two live rules keep their current defaults (on), unchanged and user-confirmed. Behaviour of a matching request is identical apart from honest usage numbers.\n- The narrowed suggestion trigger could in principle miss a future Claude Code variant that places the marker earlier. It fails *open* — the request goes upstream and is answered normally, which is the safe direction.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti\n",
