    "message": "feat(optimizer): record which local rule answered a request, and stop crediting a provider\n\nThe five local short-circuit rules answer a request inside the proxy without\ncontacting a provider. Nothing recorded that this had happened, so the whole\nlayer was unmeasurable: on a 153,198-row production log the only way to find\nout whether it had ever fired was to decompress every stored prompt and replay\nthe detectors by hand.\n\nThat measurement is what motivates this change:\n\n    title_generation_skip     3,122 fires   ~14.3M input tokens never sent\n    suggestion_mode_skip        130 fires   ~1.0M input tokens never sent\n    quota_mock                    0 fires\n    prefix_detection              0 fires\n    filepath_extraction_mock      0 fires\n\nThree separate defects, all invisible for the same reason.\n\n1. A locally-answered row named a provider. ``set_routing`` runs before the\n   intercepts, so the row recorded the provider the request *would* have gone\n   to. 3,246 phantom requests were attributed across six real providers,\n   dragging their per-provider averages with them. The route is still\n   recorded on requested_model/route_chain, so what would have happened stays\n   answerable; only the claim that it did happen is removed.\n\n2. The reported usage was invented. Every rule returned a hardcoded\n   input_tokens=100 / output_tokens=5 regardless of the request, and those\n   counts reach the client and feed its own accounting. They are counted now.\n   Measured cost of counting, cl100k on this hardware:\n\n       1,500 chars ->     405 tokens     0.5 ms\n      23,000 chars ->   6,241 tokens     7.1 ms   (median title prompt)\n      76,000 chars ->  20,628 tokens    24.4 ms   (typical suggestion prompt)\n     560,000 chars -> 152,000 tokens   145.9 ms   (largest observed)\n\n   Against the multi-second upstream round trip each match avoids, and on a\n   path that already calls this counter synchronously for web-tool requests.\n\n3. The suggestion-mode trigger scanned the whole transcript. Any user message\n   containing \"[SUGGESTION MODE:\" anywhere in history answered the request\n   with an empty string -- the worst failure this module can produce, since\n   the caller asked a real question. It now inspects only the trailing user\n   turn. Measured against all 61 real suggestion requests in the log: the\n   marker is never earlier than 97.61% into the prompt and is always followed\n   by exactly the same 1,363-character block, so narrowing loses nothing.\n\nNew: requests.optimization (the rule that answered) and\nrequests.optimization_tokens_saved (the input tokens kept off the wire), both\nNULL on an ordinary request. tokens_in/tokens_out stay NULL rather than 0 on\nan optimized row: NULL is silence and no provider spoke.\n\ncount_text_tokens is published from core.anthropic.tokens because\nget_token_count bills fixed per-message framing, which is right for a request\nand wrong for a lone reply -- it scores the empty string at 4.\n\nVerification\n- 6 mutations, each asserted applied, each caught by a named test, no\n  survivors: provider not cleared, rule not recorded, tokens_saved not\n  recorded, usage back to the constant, reply count back to the constant,\n  suggestion trigger widened to the whole transcript.\n- Migration run against the real prior schema with an existing row:\n  38 -> 42 columns, new row records the rule, the pre-existing row keeps NULL\n  and is NOT backfilled.\n- Full suite: 4,849 passed, 26 skipped, 8 failed -- all\n  tests/scripts/test_install_ps1_*, reproduced identically on unmodified\n  fork/main in the same shell.\n- ruff format, ruff check, ty: clean.\n\nDeliberately not done\n- No index on the new column. The dashboard aggregate lands in a later PR and\n  an index changes every neighbouring query's plan; it will be measured then.\n- The three never-firing rules are untouched here. They are removed in their\n  own change so this one stays about recording.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
